  "verdict_justification": "Phase 20 correctly concluded that macroeconomic variables provide no out-of-sample predictive edge for XAUUSD returns. However, the implementation contains critical accounting errors and misleading labels that require correction: (1) Benchmark F was mislabeled as 'Passive Buy-and-Hold' while incurring 516 daily round-turn executions ($154.80 in spread/slippage friction); true continuous Buy-and-Hold delivers +$710.23/oz net rather than the reported +$547.93/oz. (2) Wednesday triple-swap rollover was implemented with an off-by-one timing shift (entry_dow == 2 rather than settlement_dow == 2), shifting triple swap debits by 1 session and overstating baseline costs by $0.24 to $3.60 across models. (3) Short positions were debited -$0.12/day financing without empirical verification. After all corrections, every macro model remains net negative (-$294.54 to -$75.42/oz) and fails all promotion gates. Hence Phase 20 is partially invalid and requires formal accounting corrections, while its negative research conclusion stands.",
